d to me that under no  circumstances are we to leave the  vessels until they were in a secure and  peopled harbour the horses were in no  condition to service in such  circumstances this might occur above all  that we were going without being able to  communicate with the indians by use of  speech and without an interpreter and we  could but poorly understand ourselves  with them or learn what we desired to  know of the land that we were about to  enter a country of which we had no  account and had no knowledge of its  character of what there was in it or by  what people inhabited and besides all  this we had not food to sustain us in  wandering we knew not wither  but  to the commissary everything appeared  otherwise  and on saturday first of may the date of  this occurrence the governor ordered to  each man going with him two pounds of  biscuit and half a pound of bacon  and thus ritual we took up our march  into the country  this video is sponsored by magellan tv  the documentary streaming service  question what was the first country to  recognize the united states as a nation  a the united kingdom  b morocco or c france  yes that's right it was technically  france even though morocco did send the  first letter granting access to  morocco's ports in 1777.  thanks wikipedia and a great place to go  if your knowledge of american history is  a little rusty like me is our  documentary recommendation this month  spirit of the pony express a heartfelt  tribute to the legendary but short-lived  postal service full of historical sites  across america and eccentric characters  it's a cracking watch and magellan have  more than 3 000 other documentaries on a  wide range of topics to check out too so  click on the link in the description for  an exclusive month-long free trial for  voices of the past viewers  thanks  we of the mounted men consisted of 40.  we traveled on the allowance we had  received 15 days without finding any  other thing to eat than palmitos which  are 